# lychee exclude file — one regular expression per line.
#
# Every entry here is an *illustrative* link: documentation that shows the shape
# of a path a reader should write, not a reference to a file in this repository.
#
# These were invisible before lychee. `scripts/check-doc-dead-refs.py` checks
# backticked paths and dated ADR slugs — it does not look at markdown links at
# all — so a link to a file that does not exist sat in a skill document with
# nothing to notice it.
#
# The rule for an entry landing here: the link is an example, and the file it
# points at is not supposed to exist. A link to a file that *should* exist is a
# bug, and the fix is to correct the path, not to add it to this file.

# singularity-todo-feature-scaffold: the "### 6. <Feature>ViewModel.kt" section
# links to the MviViewModel base class to show the naming convention.
.*/singularity-todo-feature-scaffold/core/ui/MviViewModel\.kt
